{"summary": "`evaluate_subject` in `trialops/eligibility.py` already did everything requested, so I left it unchanged. I only added tests to `tests/test_eligibility.py`; the full suite passes (64 tests, up from 47).

New tests cover: a consent signed after `on` (ignored); a correct-version consent signed before `consent_valid_from` (`CONSENT_MISSING` only); a consent signed exactly on `consent_valid_from` (accepted); age and lab values just outside and exactly on the limits; a leap-day birthday in a non-leap year; exclusions matching only listed flags, case-sensitively; each required field, when missing, raising a `ValueError` that names it; and malformed values (a timestamp as `signed_on`, a consent with no version, a lab value given as a string). The existing tests already covered same-day consent, a retired wrong-version consent, reason ordering and picking the latest consent across versions.

Two existing behaviours to know about: a consent that is both too old and the wrong version gets both `CONSENT_MISSING` and `CONSENT_VERSION` (the existing tests expect this), and if two consents share the latest date, the one listed later wins."}
